  "description": "Atin decision 2026-10-01. Keep two channels: c11 send stays the plain explicit poke; the mailbox becomes the durable channel. Record both with full text, and have c11 write a live self-contained HTML page of all agent traffic. Today agents use only c11 send because mailbox push gates on shell promptIdle and never reaches a running agent (166 buffered, 2 flushed all-time), and c11 send leaves no trace in any log. Built as five parallel lanes against pinned contracts (see plan): A record every send as a tab.input_sent event and put bodies on mailbox events; B push mail when the agent is waiting, not when the shell is idle; C drain inboxes at turn boundaries through Claude, Codex and Grok hooks; D c11 writes messages.html and c11 messages view opens it; E mailbox --help fix and skill teaching. Design reference for D: the Overwatch prototype at code/overwatch/tools/mailbox-viz/. Done when one tagged build passes Atin's numbered sign-off script.",
